[Music]  so many of you have had questions about  the school year so we have been  collecting them  and wanted to take them directly to the  people in charge  joining us now is dr carla lauria who is  the chief academic officer at ccsd thank  you so much for your time this evening  we greatly appreciate that doctor  we do have several questions from our  viewers so let's begin with the first  teresa roach mchugh she wants to know  what is the district going to do about  the magnet programs  she says her daughter is in her senior  year at northwest and it's a very  hands-on program  thank you for having us and for allowing  to answer some of these questions that  are so important for so many of our  parents  distance education of course is not  ideal but it's needed  um during the current pandemic so for  magnet programs all  we understand that they are hands on and  in many cases it is important for the  kids to be  in school um but our students  will have the opportunity to engage with  the teachers  virtually our teachers are finding great  ways  to do the best they can to reach out to  the students  um allow them to participate in  activities in on online activities that  are engaging  we do know that distance education is  not ideal we want students back in  school but when it  needed a pandemic our trustees are  receiving updated health  information every 30 days they  will be determining um based on the  information we  we receive when is a good time for  all of us to be to go back to classroom  of course keeping safety  in the forum in the forefront  doctor our next question comes in from a  viewer named kelsey chatwin  she writes in what are the schedules  going to look like for preschool  and kids with ieps will students who  need help with speech  still get to see a speech teacher  yes the schedules for preschool will  look similar to  their kindergarten schedules they will  follow the normal schedule or doing that  normal hours  if the child is in half day preschool  it's going to be of course a shortened  day if it's in a full day preschool  the student will have opportunities to  engage  in two ways with the teachers one of  them is the  synchronous way we have heard that word  um  more often lately than ever but that  really means  um to be able to participate in a  face-to-face  um activity with the teacher in a live  activity with the teacher  virtually so it is just like we are  doing right now  via the technology then we are going to  be able to access the teacher directly  and also we will be able to to  learn via asynchronous um  model lessons uh which really means  uh the students engage in in their own  learning independently with activities  that have been specially  selected by the teachers to continue the  learning of the students  um students with ieps students like you  said who may need speech they will  be able to connect virtually with the  teachers  at this point um the teachers will need  to use their discretion and determine  whether they feel comfortable to come  into the school  whether they feel safe to come into the  school  and um in either work at the school  or from the school or work virtually but  they will be able to engage  in in the special needs  opportunities that they may have based  on their ieps  okay dr lorea mandy mccabe wants to know  the following she wants to know if there  will be any additional tutoring services  available yes there will be a digital  tutoring services  student services have have always been  managed at the school  level and there will be opportunities  for students to engage  in smarter group or one-on-one sessions  virtually  with their teachers as the teachers feel  the need  we're also as a district working with  different organizations  to organize probably community  organizations who may be also available  to provide services to students  and if they feel comfortable they may be  students may be able to attend those  sessions face to face dr lorea this  question comes in from scott r joseph he  writes in what is going to happen with  the credits  towards graduation  um as usual there was their online  credit retrieval options for students we  also have the nevada learning academy  and that will be functioning as normal  they have always been  virtual so that will continue our  students also  will have the ability to graduate early  from high school  if they have the credits that make them  eligible to do that  at the same time educators will be able  to reach out students in very  unique way in very individualized  manners so that they can support  students if to recover credits if that  is the case but students will continue  being able to recover credit towards  graduating  dr carla lorea joining us live on eight  news now  doctor we thank you so much for your  time and providing that information  for our viewers we do appreciate it  thank you  plans do look a little different for  private and charter schools this fall  eight news now reporter sally hatamia  spoke to principals superintendents and  ceos of a few different schools  and gives us a look at what their  learning plans involve  i think it's a challenge when you shut  down athletics and you shut down the  arts and you shut down all the after  school activities it's not just the  education it's that social piece it's  where the kids find their passion after  school when that all gets shut down it  takes a toll on everybody  the typical back to school looks a  little different for the various charter  schools  with some opting for classroom settings  while others  are staying virtual our plan really has  two options for our families one is to  come back five days a week face-to-face  and then we also have an option for  families who aren't comfortable yet  sending their kids back  we're going to tape every single class  every day and not everyone is doing  everything  exactly the same we're sponsored by  clark county school district  we made the move to online learning  and our face-to-face component was just  suspended  temporarily our board decision that was  made a little over a week ago  was to return all virtually and when it  comes to health in schools  the ceo of faith lutheran middle and  high school says it will be taken  very seriously some of the things would  include we're taking temperatures every  morning doing some health screening  we're extending passing periods we have  one-way hallways we're serving lunch  from five different places  we're not gathering for chapel every  week like we normally would in addition  desks will be cleaned between every  block and every student and teacher will  be required to wear a mask  social distance and even wear a face  shield right now our numbers show about  six percent of our students are going to  choose what we call option two to stay  home  and about 94 percent of them seem to  want to come back five days a week  superintendent at odyssey charter school  says they've been fortunate to have  scheduled their blended learning model  and feel fully equipped so we're going  to begin online  and then what we're hoping is that as  things improve  with copic 19 that we will  slowly begin to shift back into our  online  combined with our face-to-face component  of our program  and over at somerset the principal says  the goal is consistency  is that perfect for all of our families  no  no matter what we do it's not perfect  for all of our families  but we had to look at what can we do  to be consistent with our kids and even  though all plants are different  everyone has the same need for  flexibility we're going to rely on the  southern nevada health district  and or the governor and or the cdc if  they would need to completely shut us  down we'd be ready to pivot immediately  into fully remote learning if we have to  sallie jaramillo 8 news now some school  plans changed after the governor's press  conference last week  charter schools that were set to open  prior to august 24th  will now be virtual until that date and  of the 19 charter schools that are  opening  today six switched from the hybrid model  to distance learning  those are discovery charter school  aquipo academy  founders academy quest charter academy  and signature prep  an additional 19 charter schools are set  to open  the week of the 17th so far pinecrest  has switched to full  distance others tell us they are still  trying to figure out what they plan to  do  for a list on more of the private and  charter school plans check out our  website 8newsnow.com  a lot of parents scrambling with that  new information coming up don't forget  to vaccinate the shots children will  still need before school starts  up again that's next on the valley's  news leader

